<p class="legal-title">Last updated November 2, 2026</p>

<p>DocuMate is the student transaction system of the Office of the Vice President for Student Development (VPSD) of Leyte Normal University (LNU). By creating an account or using DocuMate, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the system.</p>

<h4>1. What DocuMate is for</h4>
<p>DocuMate lets students request and track VPSD forms, book visits to the office, check clearance, and download finished documents. It lets VPSD staff and University officials review, sign, issue and keep those records. It supports University procedures; it does not replace them. Where a University policy or the law says otherwise, the policy or the law prevails.</p>

<h4>2. Who may use it</h4>
<p>DocuMate is for enrolled LNU students, student organization officers, VPSD staff, and University officials the VPSD office authorizes. Anyone may use the public verification page to check a DocuMate document.</p>

<h4>3. Your account</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Register with your own true details and your own working email. That email is where password resets and notices are sent, and it can only be changed from your Profile.</li>
    <li>One person, one account. Do not use someone else's identity or account, or let anyone use yours.</li>
    <li>Keep your password private. Tell the VPSD office at once if you think someone else has used your account.</li>
    <li>Student and officer accounts must have a verified enrollment slip for the current period. If verification is not completed by the deadline, the account becomes inactive until a current slip is verified.</li>
    <li>The VPSD office may restrict or deactivate an account to protect records or the system, or when a user breaks these Terms.</li>
</ul>

<h4>4. What you submit</h4>
<p>Everything you enter or upload must be true, complete, readable and your own (or properly authorized). Do not submit altered, borrowed or falsified documents, or files that contain malware. Incorrect or misleading submissions may be returned, rejected, or referred for disciplinary action under the Student Handbook.</p>

<h4>5. Electronic signatures and sealed documents</h4>
<p>Officials may sign documents in DocuMate with their saved e-signature or through a private email link. Saving an e-signature in your Profile authorizes DocuMate to place it on documents you approve; replacing it never changes documents you already signed. These electronic signatures are recognized under the Electronic Commerce Act of 2000 (Republic Act No. 8792) and University procedures.</p>
<p>Each approval and each finished document is sealed. Once a document is completed it cannot be edited; the VPSD office can only withdraw (void) it and issue a corrected one. Never forge, copy or misuse anyone's signature, and never alter a DocuMate document. The verification page will show that an altered copy does not match its seal.</p>

<h4>6. Clearance</h4>
<p>Only authorized officers and VPSD staff may tag clearance, and only from the records they are responsible for. Falsely marking a student cleared or uncleared is a violation of these Terms and of University rules.</p>

<h4>7. AI features and the DocuMate Assistant</h4>
<p>DocuMate uses AI to read documents, flag possible problems for staff, and answer questions through the DocuMate Assistant. AI output can be wrong. It is guidance, not an official decision: staff review every transaction, and official answers come from the VPSD office and the Student Handbook. Do not enter other people's personal information, or anything unrelated to your transaction, in the Assistant.</p>

<h4>8. Acceptable use</h4>
<p>Do not try to access records or functions your role does not allow, get around security, overload or disrupt the system, collect other people's information, or use anything you see in DocuMate outside your authorized purpose. Do not share screenshots or copies of other students' records.</p>

<h4>9. Privacy</h4>
<p>How DocuMate handles personal information, including what the public verification page shows, is explained in the Privacy Policy, which forms part of these Terms.</p>

<h4>10. Availability and changes</h4>
<p>We try to keep DocuMate available but cannot promise it will always be uninterrupted or error-free, especially during maintenance or outages of the services it relies on. Features may change. When these Terms change, the new date appears at the top, and significant changes are announced in DocuMate. Continuing to use DocuMate means you accept the updated Terms.</p>

<h4>11. Consequences</h4>
<p>Breaking these Terms may lead to the restriction or deactivation of your account, rejection of affected transactions, and action under the Student Handbook, University policies, and Philippine law, including the Data Privacy Act and the Cybercrime Prevention Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10175).</p>

<h4>12. Ownership</h4>
<p>The DocuMate software, design and documentation belong to their developers and the University. Your submissions remain subject to University records rules and the Privacy Policy.</p>

